Thermo emf $E=16 T-0.04 T^2$
At inversion temperature \left(T i\right), E=0$
\therefore \quad $\begin{aligned}$0 &amp; =16 T_i-0.04 T_i^2 \\
16 T i &amp; =0.04 T_i^2 \\
T i &amp; =$\frac{16}{0.04}=$400^{{}^{{}^{\circ}}} $\mathrm{C}
\end{aligned}$Neutral temperature $T_n=\frac{T i+T}{2}T=$ Temperature of cold end T_n=$\frac{400+0}{2}=$200^{{}^{{}^{\circ}}} $\mathrm{C}
